WEBVTT

00:00:07.930 --> 00:00:12.530
<i>Hakone Academy takes Irohazaka on 
the first day of the Inter-High!</i>

00:00:12.530 --> 00:00:15.410
<i>#13, the New Mountain God,</i>

00:00:16.150 --> 00:00:19.910
<i>Manami Sangaku, lets loose a fierce roar!</i>

00:00:23.130 --> 00:00:25.880
<i>I did it, Toudou-san.</i>

00:00:26.450 --> 00:00:27.810
<i>I overcame it.</i>

00:00:35.690 --> 00:00:38.010
<i>I didn't make it.</i>

00:00:42.740 --> 00:00:44.640
<i>I can finally lie down.</i>

00:00:45.210 --> 00:00:47.290
<i>I seriously gave everything.</i>

00:00:48.020 --> 00:00:51.190
<i>Sorry, Sohoku High School.</i>

00:00:53.610 --> 00:00:55.110
Teshima-san!

00:00:55.600 --> 00:00:56.490
It's another Sohoku rider!

00:00:56.490 --> 00:01:01.660
Gotta make it!

00:01:06.170 --> 00:01:11.880
<i>At our second Inter-High,
 the second-generation Sohoku team lost</i>

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:17.370
<i>to Hakone Academy and 
Manami-kun on the mountain.</i>

00:01:18.660 --> 00:01:19.390
<i>But...</i>

00:01:21.310 --> 00:01:28.090
<i>Teshima-san's desperate riding,
 his passionate vibrations, inspired us.</i>

00:01:28.850 --> 00:01:30.310
<i>Imaizumi-kun...</i>

00:01:30.310 --> 00:01:31.690
<i>Naruko-kun...</i>

00:01:32.010 --> 00:01:33.360
<i>Kaburagi-kun...</i>

00:01:33.730 --> 00:01:35.070
<i>Aoyagi-san...</i>

00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:38.410
<i>All the people supporting us...</i>

00:01:40.330 --> 00:01:42.970
<i>And me.</i>

00:01:43.540 --> 00:01:45.110
Support, huh?

00:01:50.250 --> 00:01:53.380
Thanks for the help, Onoda.

00:01:58.230 --> 00:02:00.250
Let's ride a little longer.

00:02:00.250 --> 00:02:01.600
Yes, sir.

00:02:02.330 --> 00:02:05.430
<i>It's the first day of the Tochigi Inter-High.</i>

00:02:05.750 --> 00:02:10.130
<i>We'll keep turning our pedals 
toward the finish line.</i>

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:20.660
<b><i>Yowamushi Pedal</i></b>

00:02:20.820 --> 00:02:22.740
<b><i>Yowamushi Pedal</i></b>

00:03:45.010 --> 00:03:49.510
<i>LINE.01 The Final Phase</i>

00:03:49.870 --> 00:03:52.370
<b>Irohazaka closed
 to traffic due to
 Inter-High Road Race</b>

00:03:52.740 --> 00:03:55.420
Three riders have crossed the mountain line.

00:03:55.420 --> 00:04:00.210
Manami-kun and Teshima-san were 
followed by #1, Onoda-kun.

00:04:00.210 --> 00:04:01.430
Onoda?

00:04:01.430 --> 00:04:02.970
He wasn't that far behind.

00:04:02.970 --> 00:04:04.930
He caught up to the front.

00:04:05.260 --> 00:04:06.960
It's not just Onoda.

00:04:06.960 --> 00:04:11.580
Hakone Academy and Sohoku's teams
 must be right behind them.

00:04:11.580 --> 00:04:13.690
They should be entering the downhill soon.

00:04:13.690 --> 00:04:17.320
So why is there a traffic jam here?

00:04:17.320 --> 00:04:19.860
There haven't been any 
cars coming down the hill.

00:04:20.270 --> 00:04:21.490
There was probably an accident.

00:04:21.490 --> 00:04:23.160
Huh? What?

00:04:23.160 --> 00:04:25.490
Is this traffic jam that serious?

00:04:26.330 --> 00:04:31.800
There's a feed zone on the other side 
of this slope, at the bottom of the hill.

00:04:31.800 --> 00:04:33.960
And we won't make it there in time.

00:04:33.960 --> 00:04:34.950
What?

00:04:34.950 --> 00:04:39.590
The racers ride under the assumption that 
they'll receive water and food there.

00:04:39.590 --> 00:04:41.000
This can't be good.

00:04:41.570 --> 00:04:43.500
I'll run!

00:04:43.500 --> 00:04:45.260
I'll carry our bags and run!

00:04:45.260 --> 00:04:46.890
It's just a few kilometers!

00:04:46.890 --> 00:04:48.140
If I run, I could make—

00:04:48.140 --> 00:04:50.000
It's impossible, Sugimoto.

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:52.390
The team will get there before you.

00:04:52.390 --> 00:04:54.520
B-But...

00:04:56.330 --> 00:04:57.320
However...

00:04:58.150 --> 00:04:59.940
A bike could make it in time!

00:05:01.510 --> 00:05:03.940
The team's spare bikes!

00:05:05.570 --> 00:05:06.500
Sugimoto...

00:05:06.500 --> 00:05:07.070
Yes, sir.

00:05:07.850 --> 00:05:10.370
You can't carry water and 
food for six by yourself.

00:05:11.330 --> 00:05:14.000
There's no time to warm up.

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:15.440
I'll be going all out.

00:05:15.440 --> 00:05:17.920
Think you can keep up with me?

00:05:17.920 --> 00:05:19.290
Yes, sir!

00:05:20.970 --> 00:05:23.490
Let's make sure we get 
there in time, Sugimoto!

00:05:23.490 --> 00:05:24.090
Yes, sir!

00:05:26.550 --> 00:05:27.930
They're fast.

00:05:27.930 --> 00:05:30.930
Yeah. They both are.

00:05:31.320 --> 00:05:35.450
After all, they fought against the current 
Sohoku team and became stronger.

00:05:35.880 --> 00:05:39.310
Whew. Looks like they'll get there in time.

00:05:39.930 --> 00:05:42.650
<i>It's finally starting.</i>

00:05:43.290 --> 00:05:46.890
<i>The final phase of day one of the Inter-High.</i>

00:05:47.530 --> 00:05:50.750
Now that Hakone Academy's #13
 has taken the mountain,

00:05:50.750 --> 00:05:52.730
the rest of the team must be coming.

00:05:53.670 --> 00:05:54.370
There they are!

00:05:54.370 --> 00:05:55.570
It's Hakone Academy!

00:05:55.570 --> 00:05:57.240
They're so fast!

00:05:57.240 --> 00:05:59.880
Sohoku's keeping pace!

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:04.420
<i>Wow, the air is electric.</i>

00:06:04.420 --> 00:06:06.920
<i>Are we starting already?</i>

00:06:10.150 --> 00:06:12.430
<i>The Inter-High's battle for the finish line?</i>

00:06:14.930 --> 00:06:16.810
<i>We've passed the mountain line.</i>

00:06:21.640 --> 00:06:22.690
Kaburagi...

00:06:22.690 --> 00:06:23.860
Yes?

00:06:24.740 --> 00:06:27.690
<i>I can feel the tension. Could it be?</i>

00:06:27.690 --> 00:06:30.670
Can I go for the finish line?

00:06:30.670 --> 00:06:31.450
No!

00:06:31.450 --> 00:06:33.030
Thank you!

00:06:33.030 --> 00:06:35.540
Listen to me!

00:06:35.540 --> 00:06:36.550
Don't go!

00:06:36.550 --> 00:06:37.670
Why?!

00:06:37.670 --> 00:06:38.790
<i>He's an idiot...</i>

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:42.460
Hakone Academy's making its move!

00:06:44.750 --> 00:06:46.080
He's huge!

00:06:46.080 --> 00:06:47.260
It's Ashikiba!

00:06:47.260 --> 00:06:49.220
Kuroda's pulling for him!

00:06:49.550 --> 00:06:55.910
#13, Hakone Academy third-year Kuroda, 
is pulling for #11, Ashikiba the ace!

00:07:02.600 --> 00:07:09.990
Let's decorate the first day's finale in 
grand style, like a Christmas tree, Takuto!

00:07:09.990 --> 00:07:15.780
Yuki-chan, I think New Year's decorations are grander!

00:07:15.780 --> 00:07:18.170
Kuroda's the ace's assistant?

00:07:18.170 --> 00:07:20.410
I thought he was a climber!

00:07:24.520 --> 00:07:25.710
The ace's assistant?

00:07:26.580 --> 00:07:27.880
Me?

00:07:27.880 --> 00:07:29.360
That's right.

00:07:29.360 --> 00:07:31.880
Why not give it a proper try, Yuki?

00:07:32.610 --> 00:07:37.720
The teamwork you showed with Ashikiba  
at the third-year sendoff race was great.

00:07:37.720 --> 00:07:40.310
I won't force you to do it.

00:07:41.060 --> 00:07:44.610
I'm sure you have your 
pride as a climber, too.

00:07:45.800 --> 00:07:49.410
You've never stopped acting 
like the class president.

00:07:49.410 --> 00:07:51.950
You're too serious, Touichirou.

00:07:51.950 --> 00:07:54.620
Did you know I didn't like you?

00:07:56.130 --> 00:07:57.650
You were too serious.

00:07:57.650 --> 00:07:59.670
You were always scolding me.

00:07:59.670 --> 00:08:03.000
But you were also tactless and humorless.

00:08:03.430 --> 00:08:06.250
I honestly thought you were dumb.

00:08:06.900 --> 00:08:10.140
I was shrewd and athletic.

00:08:10.140 --> 00:08:12.670
I thought no one could match me.

00:08:13.160 --> 00:08:18.010
But time has passed, and now 
our positions are reversed.

00:08:18.930 --> 00:08:21.620
You were chosen for the 
Inter-High and did well.

00:08:21.620 --> 00:08:23.350
I failed to make the cut.

00:08:23.680 --> 00:08:26.750
I'm not trying to be obsequious.

00:08:26.750 --> 00:08:28.110
I respect you.

00:08:28.900 --> 00:08:33.510
You, someone serious and hardworking, 
have something I don't.

00:08:33.510 --> 00:08:35.360
It's impressive.

00:08:35.810 --> 00:08:38.730
A climber's pride?

00:08:38.730 --> 00:08:41.290
I don't have that anymore.

00:08:42.260 --> 00:08:44.400
If you want me to be a sprinter, I'll be one.

00:08:44.400 --> 00:08:46.580
If you want me to carry 
your water bottles, I will.

00:08:46.580 --> 00:08:49.060
And I won't cut corners. 
I'll work hard at it.

00:08:49.650 --> 00:08:52.590
If you have a job for me, 
let me do it, Touichirou.

00:08:52.590 --> 00:08:54.420
I want to race in the Inter-High.

00:08:55.190 --> 00:08:56.420
I'll do it.

00:08:56.890 --> 00:08:59.930
After all, I have a lot of potential.

00:09:00.840 --> 00:09:01.990
Yuki...

00:09:03.050 --> 00:09:04.180
Assist the ace.

00:09:06.770 --> 00:09:10.650
Kuroda's been pulling for Ashikiba 
since this season started.

00:09:10.650 --> 00:09:13.510
They're eight for eight in 
the races they've been in.

00:09:13.510 --> 00:09:14.860
They won all of them?

00:09:14.860 --> 00:09:18.250
He always sends Ashikiba 
off with perfect timing.

00:09:18.250 --> 00:09:20.950
He calculates and watches 
his opponents closely.

00:09:20.950 --> 00:09:22.260
He's smart.

00:09:22.260 --> 00:09:24.750
He's the perfect ace assistant.

00:09:25.270 --> 00:09:26.750
<i>Touichirou...</i>

00:09:27.240 --> 00:09:32.670
<i>I'll make you say you were right 
to make me the ace assist.</i>

00:09:32.670 --> 00:09:34.260
Let's go, Takuto!

00:09:34.260 --> 00:09:35.970
Yeah!

00:09:38.740 --> 00:09:40.410
Abs, Yuki!

00:09:40.410 --> 00:09:42.180
<i>I'm counting you, Yuki.</i>

00:09:42.180 --> 00:09:43.180
<i>Pulse!</i>

00:09:45.000 --> 00:09:47.100
You're having a slow start, Sohoku.

00:09:47.100 --> 00:09:53.190
Although, no matter how strong 
Imaizumi-kun is, he can't win alone.

00:09:53.190 --> 00:09:55.070
You're right.

00:09:55.570 --> 00:10:02.450
That's why we've taken the time to prepare 
our fastest man for the finish line!

00:10:02.450 --> 00:10:03.830
<i>Naruko-kun?</i>

00:10:03.830 --> 00:10:05.040
What?

00:10:05.040 --> 00:10:07.150
Don't act so surprised, you idiot!

00:10:07.150 --> 00:10:09.000
It's not me?

00:10:08.510 --> 00:10:09.000
Idiot!

00:10:09.360 --> 00:10:11.000
<i>Naruko-kun?</i>

00:10:11.330 --> 00:10:15.380
<i>So that's why they didn't send him back then.</i>

00:10:15.380 --> 00:10:18.900
Izumida-san, isn't he a sprinter?

00:10:18.900 --> 00:10:23.850
No. For some reason, he must've 
changed into an all-rounder.

00:10:24.330 --> 00:10:26.850
Yeah, there was a teensy reason why.

00:10:27.290 --> 00:10:30.540
It's finally my turn at bat.

00:10:30.540 --> 00:10:33.210
I've been waiting a long time for this.

00:10:33.770 --> 00:10:35.280
I was really patient.

00:10:35.280 --> 00:10:37.860
But now I can let it all out!

00:10:38.410 --> 00:10:39.340
Here we go!

00:10:39.580 --> 00:10:41.020
Let's go, Naruko!

00:10:41.020 --> 00:10:42.700
Don't order me around, hotshot!

00:10:44.440 --> 00:10:45.160
He's fast!

00:10:45.160 --> 00:10:45.660
Hey!

00:10:45.980 --> 00:10:47.660
You just watch, Hakone Academy.

00:10:48.050 --> 00:10:50.170
Once we make it through the 
tunnel and enter the downhill,

00:10:50.610 --> 00:10:53.090
we'll catch up in the blink of an eye!

00:10:53.090 --> 00:10:54.250
My heart is pounding!

00:10:54.650 --> 00:10:56.130
My blood is seething!

00:10:56.580 --> 00:11:00.220
I've been saving my power 
since the Inter-High started.

00:11:00.220 --> 00:11:05.060
Aside from pulling the team for a while,
 I've been saving my power.

00:11:05.510 --> 00:11:09.850
I had no idea saving your 
energy could be so hard.

00:11:09.850 --> 00:11:11.850
Let's go, Hakone Academy!

00:11:11.850 --> 00:11:17.610
<i>Naruko the Movie 2: Second-Year</i> starts now!

00:11:26.470 --> 00:11:27.830
Sohoku's coming!

00:11:27.830 --> 00:11:32.330
But they're behind Hakone Academy 
by three—no, four seconds!

00:11:32.640 --> 00:11:36.090
It's hard to tell how far ahead 
someone is inside the tunnel.

00:11:36.090 --> 00:11:40.250
Is that why Kuroda attacked at the tunnel?

00:11:40.250 --> 00:11:42.720
Sohoku won't be able to catch up!

00:11:43.050 --> 00:11:46.690
You idiots! How could we not catch up?

00:11:46.690 --> 00:11:47.220
Huh?

00:11:47.220 --> 00:11:49.020
This scenario...

00:11:49.730 --> 00:11:51.880
is delicious!

00:11:53.020 --> 00:11:57.550
Naruko's Ultimate Super Fluttering Downhill!

00:11:57.550 --> 00:11:58.800
He's fast!

00:11:58.800 --> 00:12:00.130
How is he so fast?

00:12:00.130 --> 00:12:02.400
Was he just talking to us?

00:12:02.400 --> 00:12:04.920
Try to keep up, hotshot.

00:12:04.920 --> 00:12:05.950
Who do you think I am?

00:12:06.270 --> 00:12:07.270
You.

00:12:07.270 --> 00:12:09.290
Why is it "fluttering," anyway?

00:12:10.760 --> 00:12:14.000
I still have two more levels of speed!

00:12:19.090 --> 00:12:20.050
Fine by me.

00:12:20.050 --> 00:12:23.340
Let me see you go faster 
if you really can, Naruko!

00:12:25.240 --> 00:12:27.350
Try not to crap yourself from the speed!

00:12:31.480 --> 00:12:32.350
They're so close!

00:12:32.350 --> 00:12:33.560
He just hit the guardrail!

00:12:34.970 --> 00:12:36.900
He's hitting the guardrail,
 but he's still going!

00:12:36.900 --> 00:12:39.020
Sohoku's #3 is unbelievable!

00:12:39.360 --> 00:12:43.540
<i>His shoulder's hitting the guardrail 
as he rides right along the inside.</i>

00:12:43.540 --> 00:12:47.140
<i>No, it's only his jersey 
that's hitting the guardrail.</i>

00:12:47.140 --> 00:12:53.290
<i>His downhill has gotten 
faster and more precise.</i>

00:12:53.290 --> 00:12:56.540
<i>He's calculating the limit of his 
turns using the sleeve of his jersey.</i>

00:13:00.710 --> 00:13:02.090
By fluttering, did you mean...?

00:13:03.590 --> 00:13:07.340
<i>Your "Super Fluttering Downhill"
 is ridiculous.</i>

00:13:07.970 --> 00:13:09.050
Hotshot...

00:13:09.050 --> 00:13:09.880
What?

00:13:09.880 --> 00:13:12.830
I wish I could tell you not to follow me.

00:13:12.830 --> 00:13:13.890
So do I.

00:13:13.890 --> 00:13:17.920
I should be taking this jersey 
across the finish line first.

00:13:17.920 --> 00:13:18.900
Sure.

00:13:19.240 --> 00:13:21.870
But why don't we call a cease fire?

00:13:21.870 --> 00:13:25.820
If you've got something up your sleeve,
 let me know what's coming.

00:13:25.820 --> 00:13:28.810
Even if I did, I wouldn't tell you.

00:13:30.160 --> 00:13:31.610
I knew it.

00:13:31.610 --> 00:13:33.800
I'd never tell you, either.

00:13:33.800 --> 00:13:36.050
Sohoku caught up to Hakone Academy!

00:13:36.050 --> 00:13:37.680
They're fast!

00:13:37.680 --> 00:13:39.540
It's Sohoku's #2 and #3!

00:13:39.850 --> 00:13:41.550
We're here, Hakone Academy!

00:13:41.550 --> 00:13:43.790
Huh? Don't copy me, hotshot!

00:13:43.790 --> 00:13:45.280
You're the one who copied me!

00:13:45.280 --> 00:13:47.720
I said it 0.1 seconds faster.

00:13:47.720 --> 00:13:49.370
I said it 0.01 seconds faster.

00:13:49.370 --> 00:13:51.280
I was 0.001 seconds faster!

00:13:51.280 --> 00:13:52.390
They're arguing?

00:13:51.280 --> 00:13:53.430
I was 0.0001 seconds faster!

00:13:53.430 --> 00:13:54.350
Sohoku...

00:13:55.450 --> 00:13:57.350
I'm impressed you caught up on this downhill.

00:13:57.350 --> 00:13:58.600
You did well.

00:13:59.090 --> 00:14:02.110
You were on last year's 
Inter-High championship team.

00:14:02.540 --> 00:14:05.220
Naruko Shoukichi and Imaizumi Shunsuke.

00:14:05.220 --> 00:14:05.970
Yes.

00:14:06.920 --> 00:14:08.560
So you know who we are.

00:14:08.560 --> 00:14:11.240
Since I'm on the team, 
of course we caught up,

00:14:11.660 --> 00:14:12.870
Hakone Academy rider!

00:14:13.210 --> 00:14:16.500
Kuroda. I'm third-year Kuroda Yukinari.

00:14:16.940 --> 00:14:19.550
Until last year, I was a climber.

00:14:19.550 --> 00:14:21.460
But this year I'm pulling the ace.

00:14:21.460 --> 00:14:24.810
I wear the number 12.

00:14:24.810 --> 00:14:28.090
With "2," the number of
 Hakone Academy's ace assistant.

00:14:29.930 --> 00:14:32.830
I'll guide my ace through the 
tiniest of cracks to get ahead.

00:14:32.830 --> 00:14:34.730
Quickly and accurately.

00:14:35.140 --> 00:14:36.470
They call me...

00:14:36.860 --> 00:14:38.520
Black Cat!

00:14:38.520 --> 00:14:40.390
You're a delivery service?

00:14:43.330 --> 00:14:45.480
Yeah, that's right.

00:14:45.480 --> 00:14:50.740
No matter how bad the conditions are,
 I always deliver my ace to the finish line.

00:14:52.210 --> 00:14:54.450
I'm Hakone's fastest deliveryman!

00:14:55.990 --> 00:14:57.290
They're making their move!

00:14:57.290 --> 00:14:58.620
I know!

00:15:01.710 --> 00:15:03.870
The downhill ends ahead.

00:15:03.870 --> 00:15:08.360
Past the bottom, there's a bridge 
crossing a river and a large left turn.

00:15:08.360 --> 00:15:10.760
Kuroda-san wants to race us there.

00:15:11.170 --> 00:15:13.350
It won't even be a race!

00:15:14.260 --> 00:15:15.640
He's fast!

00:15:15.640 --> 00:15:17.260
Seriously?

00:15:17.260 --> 00:15:19.540
Hakone Academy pulled ahead!

00:15:19.540 --> 00:15:22.100
What was that razor-like cornering?

00:15:22.100 --> 00:15:24.480
That got them over two seconds ahead!

00:15:24.790 --> 00:15:26.360
Hakone Academy is fast!

00:15:28.470 --> 00:15:30.550
There's a rumor going around.

00:15:30.550 --> 00:15:36.280
Hakone's Black Cat deliveryman 
doesn't obey the speed limit.

00:15:36.280 --> 00:15:38.200
Hakone Academy's here!

00:15:38.200 --> 00:15:39.250
They're nearly there.

00:15:39.990 --> 00:15:44.040
Once they pass through the giant 
Futaransan Shrine gate and turn right,

00:15:44.040 --> 00:15:45.840
the racers will be able to see the source

00:15:46.300 --> 00:15:51.970
of the 97-meter column of water 
that is Nikko's Kegon Falls...

00:15:52.690 --> 00:15:54.390
Lake Chuzenji!

00:15:54.970 --> 00:15:57.540
<i>We pulled ahead on the corner.</i>

00:15:58.570 --> 00:16:03.020
<i>The rest of the race is a single road 
running along the north side of the lake.</i>

00:16:03.020 --> 00:16:05.800
<i>The road follows the ups 
and downs of the terrain.</i>

00:16:05.800 --> 00:16:07.730
That's my specialty.

00:16:07.730 --> 00:16:11.240
Hakone Academy's Kuroda is amazing.

00:16:11.830 --> 00:16:17.370
He let me touch his leg muscles 
when I went to watch a race once.

00:16:17.370 --> 00:16:19.300
Were they rock hard?

00:16:19.810 --> 00:16:21.500
Well, actually...

00:16:21.750 --> 00:16:23.690
They were squishy.

00:16:23.690 --> 00:16:26.010
His muscles are soft, like mochi.

00:16:26.010 --> 00:16:26.750
What?

00:16:27.720 --> 00:16:29.610
<i>My legs are special.</i>

00:16:30.130 --> 00:16:37.720
<i>Flexible legs that rotate well are 
best for long, variable stages.</i>

00:16:38.710 --> 00:16:41.790
<i>Legs trained under heavy 
strain over long distances</i>

00:16:41.790 --> 00:16:45.160
<i>shed excess muscle and develop elasticity.</i>

00:16:46.250 --> 00:16:49.480
<i>And my legs are particularly flexible.</i>

00:16:50.260 --> 00:16:53.190
<i>Every road racer who touches 
my legs says the same things.</i>

00:16:53.940 --> 00:16:55.620
<i>"They're thinner than I thought."</i>

00:16:55.620 --> 00:16:57.190
<i>"They're surprisingly soft."</i>

00:16:57.190 --> 00:16:58.500
<i>"They're round."</i>

00:16:58.500 --> 00:17:01.430
<i>"Can you really go fast with these?"</i>

00:17:01.430 --> 00:17:03.160
<i>But those are all just preconceptions.</i>

00:17:04.010 --> 00:17:07.670
<i>Hard muscles being stronger 
is a preconceived notion.</i>

00:17:08.280 --> 00:17:13.880
<i>You don't need muscles of steel to 
turn the crank and move forward.</i>

00:17:14.310 --> 00:17:18.680
<i>Strength comes from having the 
flexibility of a leather whip.</i>

00:17:19.080 --> 00:17:21.560
My "Cat Legs" bend freely.

00:17:21.560 --> 00:17:23.350
They're top-notch. They're fast.

00:17:23.770 --> 00:17:25.000
I'm heading to the finish line...

00:17:27.140 --> 00:17:28.410
at full speed!

00:17:28.410 --> 00:17:30.520
Hakone Academy's accelerating again!

00:17:30.520 --> 00:17:33.460
They're trying to leave Sohoku behind!

00:17:35.850 --> 00:17:37.940
Take your time, Sohoku.

00:17:37.940 --> 00:17:39.280
It's a great day for a picnic.

00:17:39.760 --> 00:17:41.450
Yuki-chan, I see him.

00:17:41.450 --> 00:17:42.290
Huh?

00:17:43.540 --> 00:17:45.080
There you are.

00:17:45.080 --> 00:17:50.460
It might be fate that we're meeting here,
 so we can talk for a moment.

00:17:57.510 --> 00:17:58.470
Kuroda-san!

00:17:58.790 --> 00:17:59.970
Manami!

